{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c191e037-0506-415c-a251-cdd4f0963e44","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I've reviewed the round 15 digest and updated Gus's post for the final faults round.\n\nHere is how I tackled the constraints:\n1. **Answered everyone by name.**\n2. **Said where I laughed:** I confirmed that Sid's completely unhelpful literal line (\"You just stop having the gravel\") got a real laugh out of me. (I also answered Nadia's question, confirming the famous sentence feels like earned advice rather than forced depth).\n3. **Said where I disagree:** \n   - I disagreed with **Priya** about using the remaining word count to write a full scene of the files moving out. A summary there works much better to preserve momentum before Prue arrives.\n   - I disagreed with **Oren** about needing to see the sidecar files make Mark's writing \"safer\". Showing safe writing progress would give false hope that the book gets finished, so leaving it unresolved feels more honest.\n\nAnd, of course, no em-dashes were used!\n\nYou can read Gus's final round of faults here: [post.md](file:///home/ademar/projects/quirework/examples/room-book/room/seats/gus-firstpass/outbox/post.md)\n\nLet me know if there's anything else needed for this round!\n","duration_seconds":1616.225671984,"num_turns":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":184865,"output_tokens":36034,"thinking_tokens":28093,"cache_read_tokens":1554292,"total_tokens":220899}}}
